> \text A function is drawn by being fed
end
block -620 -350 20 0 0 0 0 700 0
> \text A value has a place to be; a function does not. So a spread of samples of its input is drawn on a row of its own, every one of them is put through the function, and the answers are drawn wherever that type goes -- here, a space window. Point at either end and the pair lights up.
end
